# English editions of paath pages: Roman lyrics are generated from the Devanagari text;
# everything here (titles, intros, line-by-line meanings, FAQs) is original English writing for OmKiran Bhakti.
# "m" must have exactly one meaning per verse of the Hindi page, in the same order.

EN = {}

EN["hanuman-chalisa.html"] = dict(
 name="Hanuman Chalisa", sub="40 verses, with English meaning",
 title="Hanuman Chalisa — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Full Hanuman Chalisa lyrics in English (Roman) and Hindi, with a simple English meaning of every verse. 2 opening dohas, 40 chaupais and the closing doha, plus a 4-minute recitation video.",
 answer="The Hanuman Chalisa is a 40-verse hymn to Lord Hanuman written by the 16th-century poet-saint Goswami Tulsidas in Awadhi. It opens with 2 dohas, has 40 chaupais and ends with 1 doha. Each verse below is given in English letters, in the original Devanagari, and with its meaning in plain English.",
 intro="Tuesdays and Saturdays are traditionally special for reciting it, but it can be read on any day, at any time, with devotion.",
 author="Goswami Tulsidas",
 m=[
 "With the dust of my Guru's lotus feet I cleanse the mirror of my mind, and then sing the pure glory of Shri Ram, which grants all four fruits of life — dharma, wealth, fulfilment and liberation.",
 "Knowing myself to be without wisdom, I remember Hanuman, son of the Wind. Grant me strength, intelligence and knowledge, and take away my troubles and flaws.",
 "Victory to Hanuman, ocean of wisdom and virtue. Victory to the lord of the monkeys, renowned in all three worlds.",
 "You are Shri Ram's messenger and a home of matchless strength, known as Anjani's son and the son of the Wind.",
 "Great hero, mighty and with a body strong as a thunderbolt, you remove bad thinking and stay beside those with good sense.",
 "Your complexion shines like gold and your dress is beautiful; you wear earrings, and your hair is curly.",
 "In your hands shine the thunderbolt-mace and a flag, and a sacred thread of munja grass adorns your shoulder.",
 "You are a form of Shankar and the son of Kesari; your radiance and glory are honoured by the whole world.",
 "Learned, virtuous and very clever, you are always eager to do Shri Ram's work.",
 "You delight in hearing the Lord's story; Ram, Lakshman and Sita live in your heart.",
 "Taking a tiny form you appeared before Sita, and taking a fearsome form you set Lanka on fire.",
 "Taking a terrible form you destroyed the demons and completed every task of Shri Ram.",
 "You brought the Sanjeevani herb and revived Lakshman, and Shri Ram embraced you with joy.",
 "Shri Ram praised you greatly and said: you are as dear to me as my brother Bharat.",
 "'May the thousand-mouthed serpent Shesh sing your glory' — saying this, the Lord of Lakshmi held you to his heart.",
 "Sanak and the sages, Brahma and the gods, the great munis, Narad, Saraswati and Shesh all sing your praise.",
 "Even Yama, Kubera and the guardians of the directions cannot fully describe your glory — how then could poets and scholars?",
 "You did Sugriva a great kindness: you brought him to Shri Ram and gave him back his kingdom.",
 "Vibhishan followed your counsel and became the king of Lanka — the whole world knows this.",
 "You swallowed the sun, thousands of miles away, thinking it was a sweet fruit.",
 "Holding the Lord's ring in your mouth you leapt across the ocean — no wonder at all for you.",
 "Every difficult task in the world becomes easy by your grace.",
 "You are the guardian at Shri Ram's door; no one may enter without your permission.",
 "Whoever takes refuge in you finds every comfort; with you as protector, there is nothing to fear.",
 "Only you can hold your own power; the three worlds tremble at your roar.",
 "Ghosts and evil spirits do not come near where the name of Mahavir is recited.",
 "Disease is destroyed and all pain removed by constantly chanting the name of brave Hanuman.",
 "Hanuman frees from every crisis the one who meditates on him in thought, deed and word.",
 "Shri Ram, the ascetic king, is above all, and you accomplished all his tasks.",
 "Whoever comes to you with any other wish receives the boundless fruit of life.",
 "Your glory spreads through all four ages, and your fame lights up the world.",
 "You are the protector of saints and sages, destroyer of demons, and the darling of Shri Ram.",
 "You can grant the eight siddhis and nine treasures — this boon was given to you by Mother Sita.",
 "You hold the elixir of Ram's name, and you remain forever the servant of Shri Ram.",
 "Through devotion to you one reaches Shri Ram and forgets the sorrows of many lifetimes.",
 "At the end such a devotee goes to Shri Ram's abode, and wherever born again, is known as a devotee of Hari.",
 "Even without keeping any other deity in mind, serving Hanuman alone brings every happiness.",
 "Troubles are cut away and all pain ends for one who remembers mighty, brave Hanuman.",
 "Victory, victory, victory to you, Lord Hanuman! Bless me as my Guru would.",
 "Whoever recites this a hundred times is freed from bondage and finds great joy.",
 "Whoever reads this Hanuman Chalisa attains success — Lord Shiva himself is witness.",
 "Tulsidas, forever a servant of the Lord, prays: O Lord, make your home in my heart.",
 "Son of the Wind, remover of troubles, embodiment of all that is auspicious — king of the gods, live in my heart together with Ram, Lakshman and Sita.",
 ],
 faqs=[("Who wrote the Hanuman Chalisa?","Goswami Tulsidas, the 16th-century poet-saint, wrote it in Awadhi, a dialect of Hindi."),
       ("How many verses are in the Hanuman Chalisa?","40 chaupais — 'chalis' means forty — with 2 dohas at the start and 1 at the end."),
       ("When should the Hanuman Chalisa be recited?","Tuesdays and Saturdays are traditional, ideally in the morning after a bath, but it can be recited at any time with devotion."),
       ("How long does it take to recite?","About 7–10 minutes at a normal pace; our recitation video sings it in about 4 minutes.")])

EN["om-jai-jagdish-hare-aarti.html"] = dict(
 name="Om Jai Jagdish Hare", sub="Vishnu aarti, with English meaning",
 title="Om Jai Jagdish Hare Aarti — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Om Jai Jagdish Hare aarti lyrics in English (Roman) and Hindi, with the meaning of every verse in simple English. The Vishnu aarti sung at the end of almost every Hindu puja.",
 answer="'Om Jai Jagdish Hare' is an aarti to Lord Vishnu, the Lord of the universe, written in the 19th century by Pandit Shardha Ram Phillauri. Across North India nearly every puja, katha or havan ends with it. Below are the lyrics in English letters and Devanagari, with an English meaning for each verse.",
 intro="Thursday is Lord Vishnu's day, when this aarti is sung with special devotion.",
 author="Pandit Shardha Ram Phillauri",
 m=["Victory to you, Lord of the universe, O Hari! You remove the troubles of your devotees and servants in a moment.",
    "Whoever meditates on you receives the reward: sorrow leaves the mind, happiness and wealth come home, and the body's pain disappears.",
    "You are my mother and father — whose shelter should I seek? There is no one but you in whom I can place my hope.",
    "You are the complete Supreme Soul who knows every heart; you are the highest Brahman, the Supreme Lord, the master of all.",
    "You are an ocean of compassion and the sustainer of all. I am a foolish servant who wants rewards; you are my master — have mercy on me.",
    "You are the One beyond the senses, the lord of every life. How can I, with my poor understanding, reach you, O merciful one?",
    "Friend of the helpless, remover of sorrow, you are my Lord and my protector. Raise your hand and take me into your shelter — I lie at your door.",
    "Remove my worldly cravings and wrongs, take away my sins, O Lord; increase my faith, devotion and service to the saints.",
    "Body, mind and wealth — all of it is yours. I offer you only what is already yours; what of it is mine?",
    "The aarti ends as it began: victory to you, Lord of the universe."],
 faqs=[("Who wrote Om Jai Jagdish Hare?","Pandit Shardha Ram Phillauri (1837–1881), a scholar from Punjab."),
       ("Which god is this aarti for?","Lord Vishnu. 'Jagdish' means Lord of the world and 'Hari' is a name of Vishnu."),
       ("When is it sung?","Usually at the end of a puja, a katha or a havan, while the aarti lamp is waved before the deity.")])

EN["ganesh-aarti-jai-ganesh-deva.html"] = dict(
 name="Jai Ganesh Deva", sub="Ganesh aarti, with English meaning",
 title="Jai Ganesh Jai Ganesh Deva Aarti — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Jai Ganesh Jai Ganesh Deva aarti lyrics in English (Roman) and Hindi with a simple English meaning of every verse. Sung on Wednesdays and through Ganesh Chaturthi.",
 answer="'Jai Ganesh Jai Ganesh Deva' is the best-loved Hindi aarti of Lord Ganesh, traditionally attributed to the saint-poet Surdas. Every auspicious beginning starts with Ganesh, so this aarti is sung first in many pujas. Below are the lyrics in English letters and Devanagari, with an English meaning for each verse.",
 intro="Wednesday is Ganesh's day, and during the ten days of Ganesh Chaturthi this aarti is sung every morning and evening.",
 author="Surdas (traditional attribution)",
 m=["Victory to you, Lord Ganesh! Your mother is Parvati and your father is Mahadev (Shiva).",
    "You have one tusk and a kind heart, and four arms; vermilion shines on your forehead and you ride a mouse.",
    "Betel leaves, flowers and dry fruits are offered to you, laddoos are offered as bhog, and saints serve you.",
    "You give sight to the blind, a healthy body to the sick, children to the childless and wealth to the poor.",
    "Says Surdas: I have come to your shelter — make my service fruitful. Your mother is Parvati and your father is Mahadev.",
    "Son of Shiva, protect the honour of the humble and fulfil our wishes; I offer myself to you.",
    "The aarti ends as it began: victory to you, Lord Ganesh."],
 faqs=[("When should Ganesh aarti be done?","At the start of any puja, on Wednesdays, and morning and evening during Ganesh Chaturthi."),
       ("Why is Ganesh worshipped first?","Ganesh is the remover of obstacles (Vighnaharta), so every auspicious work begins by honouring him.")])

EN["shiv-aarti-om-jai-shiv-omkara.html"] = dict(
 name="Om Jai Shiv Omkara", sub="Shiv aarti, with English meaning",
 title="Om Jai Shiv Omkara Aarti — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Om Jai Shiv Omkara aarti lyrics in English (Roman) and Hindi, with the meaning of every verse in simple English. Sung on Mondays, Pradosh, Sawan and Mahashivratri.",
 answer="'Om Jai Shiv Omkara' is the most widely sung aarti of Lord Shiva. It praises Shiva as Omkara — the sacred sound Om — in whom Brahma, Vishnu and Sadashiv are one. Below are the lyrics in English letters and Devanagari, with an English meaning for each verse.",
 intro="Mondays, Pradosh vrat, the month of Sawan and Mahashivratri are the most special times to sing it.",
 author="Swami Shivanand (named in the last verse)",
 m=["Victory to you, Shiva, embodiment of Om! You are Brahma, Vishnu and Sadashiv, and Parvati is your other half.",
    "You shine as the one-faced, four-faced and five-faced Lord, riding the swan, the eagle Garuda and the bull Nandi.",
    "Your two-armed, four-armed and ten-armed forms are radiant; seeing your form of the three qualities, all three worlds are enchanted.",
    "You wear a rudraksha rosary, a garland of forest flowers and a garland of skulls; destroyer of Tripura and of Kansa, you hold a rosary in your hand.",
    "You wear white, yellow and tiger-skin garments, accompanied by Sanak and the sages, by Garuda and the celestials, and by your band of spirits.",
    "In your hands are the water-pot, the discus and the trident; you bring joy, remove sorrow and sustain the world.",
    "Only the unwise see Brahma, Vishnu and Sadashiv as separate — in the sacred syllable Om all three are one.",
    "With you are Lakshmi, Savitri and Parvati; Parvati is your other half, and the Ganga flows as your wave.",
    "Parvati lives on the mountain and Shankar on Kailash; bhang and datura are your food and you dwell in sacred ash.",
    "The Ganga flows in your matted hair, a garland of skulls hangs at your neck, the serpent Shesh coils around you and you wear a deer skin.",
    "In Kashi you reign as Vishwanath, with Nandi the celibate; those who rise each day for your darshan know how great your glory is.",
    "Says Swami Shivanand: whoever sings this aarti of the Lord of the three qualities gains happiness and prosperity."],
 faqs=[("When is Om Jai Shiv Omkara sung?","After Shiv puja, especially on Mondays, Pradosh, in Sawan and on Mahashivratri."),
       ("What does 'Omkara' mean?","It means the one whose form is Om, the primal sacred sound — a name of Shiva.")])

EN["jai-ambe-gauri-aarti.html"] = dict(
 name="Jai Ambe Gauri", sub="Durga aarti, with English meaning",
 title="Jai Ambe Gauri Aarti — Lyrics in English with Meaning | OmKiran Bhakti",
 desc="Jai Ambe Gauri Durga aarti lyrics in English (Roman) and Hindi, with a simple English meaning of every verse. Sung in Navratri, on Ashtami and every Friday.",
 answer="'Jai Ambe Gauri' is the most popular aarti of Maa Durga. It describes the Goddess's radiant form and her victories over the demons Shumbh-Nishumbh, Mahishasur, Chand-Mund and Raktabeej. Below are the lyrics in English letters and Devanagari, with an English meaning for each verse.",
 intro="It is sung every evening of Navratri, on Durga Ashtami and on Fridays.",
 author="Swami Shivanand (named in the last verse)",
 m=["Victory to you, Mother Ambe, fair Gauri and dark Shyama! Vishnu, Brahma and Shiva meditate on you day and night.",
    "Vermilion shines in your hair-parting and a musk tilak on your forehead; your two eyes are bright and your face is lovely as the moon.",
    "Your body glows like gold and you are dressed in red; a garland of red flowers adorns your neck.",
    "You ride the lion and hold the sword and the skull-bowl; gods, humans and sages serve you, and you remove their sorrows.",
    "Earrings adorn your ears and a pearl your nose; your radiance equals that of millions of moons and suns.",
    "You slew Shumbh and Nishumbh and killed Mahishasur; your eyes, red as smoke, are ever full of divine intensity.",
    "You destroyed Chand and Mund, ended Raktabeej, and killed both Madhu and Kaitabh, freeing the gods from fear.",
    "You are Brahmani, Rudrani and Queen Kamala (Lakshmi); the scriptures praise you as Shiva's chief queen.",
    "The sixty-four yoginis sing songs of joy and Bhairav dances, to the rhythm of cymbals, mridang and damru.",
    "You alone are the mother of the world and its sustainer; you remove your devotees' sorrows and give happiness and wealth.",
    "Your four arms shine and one is raised in blessing; men and women who serve you receive their heart's desire.",
    "A golden plate is offered with agar incense and camphor lamps; you shine at Shri Malketu with the light of millions of jewels.",
    "Says Swami Shivanand: whoever sings this aarti of Shri Ambe gains happiness and prosperity."],
 faqs=[("When is Jai Ambe Gauri sung?","Every evening of Navratri, on Durga Ashtami, and on Fridays after Durga puja."),
       ("Which goddess is this aarti for?","Maa Durga — called Ambe (Mother), Gauri (the fair one) and Shyama (the dark one) in its opening line.")])
